    "## Exercise solution\n",
    "\n",
    "In class we judged each prompt by reading one answer. Here every experiment runs on a small **labelled test set**, so zero-shot and few-shot variants can be compared by numbers (accuracy, format compliance) instead of impressions. Everything uses `gpt-3.5-turbo` at `temperature=0` so the runs are reproducible.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Movie facts:** does few-shot formatting work, and does it push the model to *invent* answers for films that don't exist?\n",
    "2. **Tricky sentiment:** sarcasm, negation and mixed reviews; zero-shot vs. balanced shots vs. *biased* shots.\n",
    "3. **Ticket routing with invented codes:** a task the model cannot know without examples. Instructions vs. shots in the system prompt vs. shots as user/assistant turns."
